WEBVTT

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.980
…turns whatever you hand it into a
finished HTTP response.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.140
The flow branches on the type of the body.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.200
A string just gets a charset,

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.520
while a plain object is handed off to
res.json instead of being sent directly.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.220
Everything else moves on to compute
Content-Length

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.277
and an ETag, before the final status check

00:00:38.277 --> 00:00:40.480
decides whether the body actually gets
sent.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.140
This switch is the entry point.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.900
A string falls back to Content-Type HTML,
unless one is already set,

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.153
in which case Express only adds a UTF-8
charset.

00:00:51.153 --> 00:00:53.660
A null body becomes an empty string,

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.260
a Buffer-like value gets Content-Type bin…
